    "why": "the paper's lattice vectors sit at -30/+30 deg (A1 = [sqrt(3)/2, -1/2] a in QuantumHallVMC); this package's Torus puts A1 along (1,0).  The frames differ by a 30 deg rotation, so the paper's x = (1,0) is the direction of G1+G2 here -- a reciprocal-lattice (Bragg) direction, which is why a cut along it passes through Q_WC.  The torus's own first Cartesian axis is 30 deg away and its momenta never reach Q_WC."
